-- title:
--   Grid reading of Gauss-order differences on the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, let $e_w, e_K \ge 1$ be natural numbers and $e = e_w e_K$. Let $x, x'$ be nonzero elements of the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)`, the quotient of $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ (two-variable multivariate power series) by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \varpi^{e}$, each presented in normal form: pairs $ab = (a,b)$ and $ab' = (a',b')$ of one-variable power series with $b$, $b'$ of zero constant coefficient, such that the class of `inU a + inV b` is $x$ and the class of `inU a' + inV b'` is $x'$, where `inU`, `inV` place a one-variable series along the $X_0$-, resp. $X_1$-axis. Throughout, the valuation used is $w \mapsto r \cdot \mathrm{addVal}_W(w)$ in $\mathbb{N}\infty$ for a scale $r$; `repGaussOrder v E t F` is $\inf_d (v(\text{coeff}_d F) + \mathrm{annulusWeight}\,E\,t\,d)$, `gaussOrder v π E t x` is the supremum of `repGaussOrder v E t F` over representatives $F$ of $x$, `dominantIndices v E t ab` is the set of $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $v(\mathrm{nfCoeff}\,ab\,n) + \mathrm{annulusWeight}\,E\,t\,(\mathrm{nfExponent}\,n)$ equal to `repGaussOrder v E t (inU ab.1 + inV ab.2)`, and `circleIndexDrop v E t ab` is the truncated difference $\sup - \inf$ of that set. The off-grid hypothesis assumes: for all naturals $r \ge 1$ and $s$ with $0 < s < re$ such that $s$ is not of the form $r(e - d e_K)$ for some $d \le e_w$, the index drops `circleIndexDrop` at scale $r$, total $re$ and depth $s$ agree for $ab$ and $ab'$. Let $\varphi : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{Z}$ be given by $\varphi(t) = (\mathrm{gaussOrder}\,t\,x).\mathrm{toNat} - (\mathrm{gaussOrder}\,t\,x').\mathrm{toNat}$ at scale $1$ and total $e$, and let $G : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{Z}$ be given by $G(d) = (\varphi(e - d e_K) - \varphi(e))/e_K$ (integer division). Then: $e_K \mid \varphi(e - d e_K) - \varphi(e)$ for all $d \le e_w$; for every $d$ with $1 \le d < e_w$, $(G(d) - G(d-1)) - (G(d+1) - G(d))$ equals the difference of the index drops of $ab$ and $ab'$ at depth $e - d e_K$; $G(1) - G(0)$ equals minus the difference of the suprema of the dominant-index sets at depth $e$, and also $-(\varphi(e) - \varphi(e-1))$; and $G(e_w) - G(e_w - 1)$ equals minus the difference of the infima of the dominant-index sets at depth $0$, and also $-(\varphi(1) - \varphi(0))$.
--
--   This is the grid form of the Gauss-order comparison on the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \varpi^{e})$: agreement of the circle index drops of two normal forms at all depths off the grid $e - d e_K$ forces the difference of their integer Gauss orders to be piecewise affine in blocks of length $e_K$, with second differences and end slopes read off from dominant indices. It is obtained from the scale-one case of the slope-drop/index-drop comparison [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.slopeDrop_sub_eq_circleIndexDrop_sub_of_forall_circleIndexDrop_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.slopeDrop_sub_eq_circleIndexDrop_sub_of_forall_circleIndexDrop_eq), and feeds the per-node Gauss-order datum used in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_slopeDrop_eq_sum_div_depth_of_sum_div_reduceFst_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_slopeDrop_eq_sum_div_depth_of_sum_div_reduceFst_eq).
